  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,dx\\,dy=$",
  "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{3y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{3y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(\\frac{1}{3}(3y)^{3}+(3y){y}^{2})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(9{y}^{3}+3{y}^{3})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}12{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}12{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[3{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3(3)^{4} \\\\  & =3(81) \\\\  & =243\\end{aligned}\n$$",
